    <node id="&quot;23-2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"23-2 是错误记录的唯一标识符，用于追踪该特定学生提交的错误答案和相关分析数据。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29266653556f4758c4fbea2541c63207</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;乘2操作&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"乘2操作是小红被允许执行的唯一操作，即将选定非空区间内所有元素的值翻倍，用于调整数组极差。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29266653556f4758c4fbea2541c63207</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGRAM SEGMENT 2/2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Program Segment 2/2 is a portion of the student's submitted code that outputs coordinate pairs for adjacent swaps, likely part of a sequence of operations to transform the matrix, but contains a logical or syntactic flaw leading to incorrect output."&lt;SEP&gt;Program Segment 2/2 is a critical portion of a student-submitted C++ solution in a programming competition context, specifically designed to address the “双生数组” (twin array) problem. Its primary function is to generate and output coordinate pairs representing adjacent swap operations required to transform a given array into a valid twin array with the minimum number of swaps. This segment constitutes the output-generating component of a larger algorithmic framework that theoretically relies on median-based optimization logic—including median selection, computation of absolute differences from the median, and conditional branching based on array length and value distribution—to minimize total transformation cost.

Despite its intended role, Program Segment 2/2 contains critical logical errors that render the overall solution incorrect. These include: (1) flawed median computation, particularly when multiple candidate medians exist; (2) incorrect summation of absolute differences from the median; (3) improper handling of edge cases related to array parity (even/odd length) and value distribution; and (4) inadequate integration with preceding algorithmic steps, resulting in incomplete or inconsistent state propagation. While the segment correctly structures output in the form of paired swap coordinates and includes standard I/O optimizations and a loop for multiple test cases, the underlying sequence of operations it produces is invalid. It may appear to output coordinate pairs, but these pairs do not correspond to a valid transformation path that achieves the required twin array configuration, leading to partial or wholly incorrect results.

Additionally, the segment fails to enforce necessary constraints or account for key problem conditions, and its implementation of the matrix/array conversion logic is fundamentally flawed. As a result, although it is structured as the final output phase of the solution, its erroneous logic directly causes the program to produce output that does not meet the problem’s requirements. Consequently, Program Segment 2/2 is identified as the primary source of failure in the student’s submission, undermining the correctness of the entire algorithm despite its syntactic correctness and superficial adherence to output format.&lt;SEP&gt;"Program Segment 2/2 is a specific part of the student’s code that handles the final output of swap operations, including assertion checks on operation count and formatting output pairs of coordinates for adjacent swaps."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6d2aa75d8324c591292a5206cbd69bde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ac191ac64f16e456c655d4b8863811&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56cf64b248d90f79e1afa9d0cd84c04a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44c8edff064a63bf1c338d7c234b2385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c34d00a1cb1d7916cefb78fbc43896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d7c8c700f1653b2de9c2e270fef6e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29266653556f4758c4fbea2541c63207&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fe6cf8d6835af29afa5ade64370e360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29764514e79d905f57239a2bf826b46d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8571d78ef0982dfe0d6ef86e585cbe98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79af8c07e093eeaf2a8b54738698e7af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31863a3502540c31035499a1b63c97c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e091fd25a6ba2509fa168c85c52636ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70a2665d10418a7ca4b53ae850057cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4c926060a3af4a149ab3816fc63a59e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d855de4fc3c8066acae7529422e672d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef1f71a373fc41a4b61f69de3413bf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7230c75a37c25448800f6f28d89050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d300103154c5f70514a4d86cc50a94df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1~N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1~n 表示排列中允许使用的整数范围，即从1到n的连续整数集合，是构造合法排列的数值域。"&lt;SEP&gt;"1~n 表示整数范围从1到n，是构造排列的合法数值域，每个整数必须恰好出现一次，构成排列的基础约束。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;井然有序之窗&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"井然有序之窗是该排列构造问题的标题，象征着在约束条件下寻找有序排列的挑战性任务。"&lt;SEP&gt;"井然有序之窗是该问题的标题或主题名称，象征着在约束条件下构建有序排列的挑战与目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"井然有序之窗是题目名称，代表一个构造满足区间约束的排列的算法问题场景。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;[L_I,R_I]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"[l_i,r_i] 是第 i 个位置元素的取值范围约束，每个位置 i 必须分配一个落在该区间内的整数，是问题的核心限制条件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i,r_i] 是第 i 个位置元素的取值范围约束，每个约束定义了该位置可放置整数的下界和上界，是问题的核心输入条件。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T is a struct type defined in the student’s C++ code to encapsulate the left bound (l), right bound (r), and original index (id) of each constraint, serving as a data structure to manage input constraints for the permutation problem."&lt;SEP&gt;"T 是学生程序中定义的结构体类型，用于存储每个位置的左边界 l、右边界 r 和原始索引 id，是算法数据结构的核心组成部分。"&lt;SEP&gt;"t 是题目要求构造的目标字符串，长度为 n，仅由小写字母组成，其可爱度需恰好等于 m。"&lt;SEP&gt;"t 是题目要求构造的目标字符串，长度为 n，仅由小写字母组成，其可爱度需恰好等于 m。"&lt;SEP&gt;"T is a variable in the student program representing the number of test cases, likely referring to a participant or contestant in a programming competition context, implicitly associated with the problem solver."&lt;SEP&gt;"T is a variable in the student program representing the number of test cases, used to control the loop that invokes the solve() function. It is an implicit participant in the computational process described in the problem."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4f71a436c68bda6c051ade04f84d6c77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae03b8ab8904bfd565e3a28acd596fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7638980c6db214619f264bda3c98a5b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bbd9f3652366c894d3ef5e4694e35b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "M" (uppercase) is a static, constant integer universally defined in computational programs as 200,007 (2×10⁵ + 7). It serves exclusively as a fixed upper bound for memory allocation in algorithmic implementations, particularly in grid-based problems such as Breadth-First Search (BFS). "M" is not a variable input but a conservative, implementation-level safeguard used to preallocate arrays (e.g., `a[M]`) to ensure sufficient and safe memory space across diverse problem instances. Although it may appear in contexts involving 2D grid maps—such as battlefield simulations with abilities like "Dragon’s Breath"—it does not represent actual grid dimensions; its role is purely structural and unrelated to any problem-specific inputs.

In contrast, the entity "m" (lowercase) is a dynamic, context-dependent parameter whose meaning varies significantly across different computational domains. In grid-based algorithmic problems, "m" represents the actual number of columns in a 2D grid, working alongside "n" (the number of rows) to define the horizontal dimension of the computational space; its value is derived directly from the problem’s input and varies per instance. In the domain of string algorithms and the concept of “可爱度” (cuteness), "m" denotes the target cuteness value, defined as the maximum length k such that there exists a contiguous substring of length k within a string t that is also a subsequence of t; in this context, "m" acts as a combinatorial constraint used to evaluate whether a constructed string satisfies a specified cuteness criterion, often determining binary outputs like "YES" or "NO". In a transformation problem centered on small L’s objective, "m" represents the target number that small L wishes to convert the input number "n" into, serving as the endpoint or desired final state of an operation. Additionally, in another context, "m" is the number of independent queries to be processed for a given permutation, each requiring position tracking after subinterval sorting, further illustrating its role as a variable input tied to specific algorithmic tasks.

Although "M" and "m" may appear visually similar and occasionally co-occur in the same codebases—particularly in grid-related algorithms—they are fundamentally distinct entities. "M" is a fixed, universal constant for memory management, while "m" is a variable whose meaning shifts depending on context: it may represent grid columns</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5df2edc3d03ec6c5e1b9a6d2ff7905f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d887a2fa6fff76122dbcba92f32c0d9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411bbe91994001030c7a545311f4d2a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd5a87d368619780b9c83a36a26e8d95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d177fa42f88e3250bf9921ff21987ec2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67a35ea6ed4e42eb7c4874b218ee041d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f24131db9a2e06f7a88e10188152d99d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-435d0b64fef9c51a64d020305df4c4a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f71a436c68bda6c051ade04f84d6c77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ea1f9429252e70930605371d38b928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d58149e2705f5337a0bc1e192ab33a56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca7b7c2c9549b0f15b3ed9c255cd57c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180c6e0fe94889fc71026468d48a172f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8571d78ef0982dfe0d6ef86e585cbe98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d77cdcffc291f16acc127cdfe41569&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79af8c07e093eeaf2a8b54738698e7af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31863a3502540c31035499a1b63c97c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82ae2ff0e583348ae265216d143270fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb4bd7875d45de235db605ada816662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa7949c55def1b07cb22840b26c2d9a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34b609ebf637b7a586a64207000b2d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bbd9f3652366c894d3ef5e4694e35b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89dd6bd1e7fef4152822627f117d0a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae03b8ab8904bfd565e3a28acd596fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ab3ebf5f1287dbbf9a2ec35fad95eea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-325b730cedcf46c053439807511ce0ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2da9ecfa854ec125c90cf41bc3e549e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22dbdf1f3163e7e66ae88a5409cc589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7638980c6db214619f264bda3c98a5b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c43422d516179991d5c796063c71f443</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANS[M]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ans 数组用于存储最终分配给每个位置的排列值，其索引对应原始输入顺序，是算法输出的关键数据结构。"&lt;SEP&gt;"ans[M] 是存储最终排列结果的数组，根据排序后的约束将数值 l 依次分配至对应原始位置 id。"&lt;SEP&gt;"ans[M] is an array in the student program that stores the final assigned values for each position in the permutation, indexed by original position id."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::SORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"std::sort 是 C++ 标准库中的排序函数，被学生程序用于按区间左端点和右端点排序，但比较逻辑不完整，可能引发错误顺序。"&lt;SEP&gt;"std::sort 是学生程序中用于按 l 升序、r 升序对区间约束进行排序的事件，是贪心策略实施的前提步骤。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L = 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"l = 1 initializes the smallest available integer to be assigned, starting from 1 and incrementing as values are allocated, representing the greedy selection pointer."&lt;SEP&gt;"l = 1 是贪心算法中当前待分配的最小可用整数，从1开始递增，用于尝试满足每个区间的最小可行值。"&lt;SEP&gt;"l 是贪心分配过程中当前可使用的最小可用整数，初始为1，随分配递增，是算法正确性的关键变量。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::CIN &gt;&gt; N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"std::cin &gt;&gt; n 是程序读取排列长度 n 的输入事件，启动整个构造过程的初始步骤。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::CIN &gt;&gt; L &gt;&gt; R&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"std::cin &gt;&gt; l &gt;&gt; r 是程序逐个读取每个位置 i 的区间约束 [l_i, r_i] 的输入事件，构建问题实例。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L &gt;= A[I].L &amp;&amp; L &lt;= A[I].R&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"该条件判断是贪心分配的核心逻辑，用于决定当前最小可用整数 l 是否可分配给第 i 个区间，但未处理后续冲突，是错误根源。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;输出 -1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"当 l &gt; n 时程序输出 -1，表示无法构造满足所有约束的排列，是算法失败的输出事件。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ab26ec20fcd79dc385eb33e508c23dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;构造排列问题&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"构造排列问题是一个算法挑战事件，要求生成一个 1 到 n 的排列，使得每个位置 i 的元素落在给定区间 [l_i, r_i] 内，是本文本的核心任务。"&lt;SEP&gt;"构造排列问题是一个算法竞赛类事件，要求生成一个 1 到 n 的排列，使得每个位置 i 的元素落在指定区间 [l_i, r_i] 内，是学生程序试图解决的核心任务。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;[L_I, R_I]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'[l_i, r_i]' denotes the inclusive interval constraint for the i-th position in the permutation, defining the allowable value range for each index in the array."&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] denotes the inclusive range constraints for each position i in the permutation, defining valid value boundaries for elements. These intervals are central to the problem’s logic and are standard in Chinese algorithmic problem design, often tested in programming contests."&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] 是第 i 个位置允许取值的闭区间范围，每个位置必须分配一个落在该区间内的整数，是排列构造的硬性约束条件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] 是第 i 个位置允许的数值范围约束，定义了排列中每个位置可填入数字的上下界，是问题的关键输入条件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] is the inclusive integer interval from which each element a_i of the sequence is independently and uniformly randomly generated, defining the range of possible values for each position."&lt;SEP&gt;"[l_i, r_i] denotes the inclusive integer interval within which each element a_i of the sequence is independently and uniformly randomly generated, forming the probabilistic basis for computing the expected value."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-52425facb0b31d12436db806ca0992de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-643a1dae351fde67dd0b6b4bafe4269b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1 ~ N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1 ~ n is the universal value domain for valid permutations, representing the integers from 1 to n that must each appear exactly once. This range is a foundational concept in Chinese competitive programming and defines the solution space for the permutation problem."&lt;SEP&gt;"1 ~ n 表示排列中允许使用的整数范围，即从 1 到 n 的连续整数，是排列构造问题的核心数值域。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M = 3E5 +7&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M is a constant defining the maximum array size in the student’s code, set to accommodate up to 300,000 constraints, reflecting standard memory allocation practices in Chinese competitive programming environments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIGNED MAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The main function entry point in the C++ program, where the computation logic is executed and the result is printed, marking the execution context of the error."&lt;SEP&gt;"signed main is the entry point function in the student’s C++ program, written using 'signed' instead of 'int' for compatibility with certain online judges common in China’s programming contest scene."&lt;SEP&gt;"signed main是学生程序的主函数入口，控制程序流程，包括读取测试用例数量T并循环调用solve函数。"&lt;SEP&gt;"signed main 是 C++ 程序的入口函数，使用 signed int 作为返回类型，是学生代码结构的一部分，但因前面错误未能正常执行。"&lt;SEP&gt;"signed main is the entry point function in a C++ program, indicating the start of execution for the code snippet that computes a value based on variables Min, Cnt, x, and y."&lt;SEP&gt;"signed main is the C++ entry point function used in the student's code, indicating the program's execution start point with a signed integer return type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d58149e2705f5337a0bc1e192ab33a56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e307f6e0f75e0c72f6c263b74efaa1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2da9ecfa854ec125c90cf41bc3e549e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22dbdf1f3163e7e66ae88a5409cc589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b590abbdea60c545ca54c73ea12cc6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4655c44a0c410e0c718d92b308d741b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1 \SIM N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'1 \sim n' represents the range of integer values (1 to n) that must be used exactly once in the permutation, forming the universal domain of valid elements for the problem."&lt;SEP&gt;"1 \sim n 表示排列中允许使用的整数范围，即从1到n的连续整数，是构造合法排列的核心数值约束。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T{INT L, R, ID}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T 是学生程序中定义的结构体，用于存储每个位置的左边界 l、右边界 r 和原始索引 id，是算法数据组织的核心单元。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M = 3E5 + 7&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M 是学生程序中定义的常量，用于分配数组大小，表示程序设计时预设的最大输入规模，体现工程实现的边界假设。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::SORT(A + 1, A + 1 + N, [](T A, T B) { RETURN A.L &lt; B.L ? A.L &lt; B.L : A.R &lt; B.R; })&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"该排序逻辑按左边界 l 升序、右边界 r 升序对区间进行预处理，是贪心算法的基础步骤，但未考虑覆盖完整性导致错误。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;第 I 个元素&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"第 i 个元素指排列中第 i 个位置（1 ≤ i ≤ n）的值，每个位置需满足其专属范围 [l_i, r_i] 的约束。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;排列&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"排列 (permutation) is a sequence of integers from 1 to n with no duplicates, forming the core data structure manipulated in the problem."&lt;SEP&gt;"排列是指由 1 到 n 的整数构成、无重复、顺序任意的数组，是本问题要求构造的目标结构。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4bbd9f3652366c894d3ef5e4694e35b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;重复元素&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"重复元素是指排列中出现多次的数字，违反排列定义，是程序必须避免的错误状态。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;超出范围的数&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"超出范围的数是指分配给某位置的值不在其 [l_i, r_i] 区间内，违反约束条件，是程序错误的直接表现。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::SORT(...)&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-5cfc0f9443b7ad1fe6055d788e835294</data>
      <data key="d1">"学生程序依赖该排序逻辑对区间进行预处理，是贪心策略的前置步骤，但设计不完善导致错误。"</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;贪心算法&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"贪心算法是学生程序采用的求解策略，通过按左端点排序后依次分配最小可用整数，但因未考虑右端点约束的全局性而失败。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANS[A[I].ID] = L&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"该语句是学生程序中核心的赋值逻辑，试图将当前最小可用整数 l 分配给第 a[i].id 个位置，但未验证后续约束是否可满足。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L++&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"l++ 是递增当前可用最小整数的操作，用于贪心分配，但缺乏回溯机制，导致局部最优无法保证全局解。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e99c195bf139756748ff95a63861cbef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\{2,3,1,5,4\}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\{2,3,1,5,4\} is an example of a valid length-5 permutation, used to illustrate correct output format and adherence to the problem's constraints."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\{1,2,2\}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\{1,2,2\} is an example of an invalid permutation due to duplicate elements, used to clarify the requirement that each integer must appear exactly once."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\{1,3,4\}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\{1,3,4\} is an example of an invalid permutation because it omits integers and includes values outside the 1~n range, highlighting the need for completeness and correct bounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T{INT L , R , ID;}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T is a struct definition in the student program used to store the left bound, right bound, and original index of each constraint, forming a key data structure for the algorithm."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STD::SORT(A + 1 , A + 1 + N , [](T A , T B) { RETURN A.L &lt; B.L; })&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This sorting event organizes the constraints by their left bound (l) in ascending order, a critical step in the greedy algorithm to assign smallest available values first."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IF(L &gt;= A[I].L &amp;&amp; L &lt;= A[I].R) ANS[A[I].ID] = L ,L ++;&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This conditional assignment event attempts to assign the smallest available integer l to position a[i].id if it lies within the constraint [l_i, r_i], then increments l — the core flawed logic of the program."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6dde8d5dace842a3db295bc3a2b69c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;排列构造问题&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"排列构造问题是一个算法挑战，要求构造一个长度为 n 的排列，使得第 i 个元素落在给定区间 [l_i, r_i] 内，且每个数字 1~n 恰好使用一次。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;算法竞赛&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"算法竞赛是一种以解决编程问题为目标的竞技活动，排列构造问题常见于此类竞赛，如 NOI、ACM 等，强调逻辑与效率。"&lt;SEP&gt;"算法竞赛是该题目所处的背景活动，通常在中国的高中或大学编程竞赛中出现，要求选手在时间与操作限制下设计高效算法解决数学构造问题。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06373e967b229fd23b64bfbbc0860861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;排序算法&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"排序算法是学生程序中使用的关键步骤，通过按区间左端点排序来贪心分配数值，是解法的核心逻辑。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;贪心策略&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"贪心策略是学生程序采用的解题方法，即按区间顺序从小到大分配最小可用数字，但未处理所有边界情况导致错误。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2025-01-21 14:55:12&quot;">
