    <node id="&quot;小苯&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"小苯是一个学生或参与者，面对一个算法问题，需要计算数组中满足 a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j) 的元素对数量。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯是题目中的主角，获得一个整数数组并试图计算满足 a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j) 的元素对数量。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯是题目中的主角，获得一个由n个整数构成的数组，并试图计算满足a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)的元素对的数量。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯是题目中的主角，拿到一个由n个整数构成的数组，并试图计算满足a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)的元素对数量。"&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯是题目中的主角，获得一个由n个整数构成的数组，并试图计算满足a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)的元素对数量。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0f831b89c29a24b6f937f910e69eb76a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OI-WIKI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"OI-Wiki 是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki 是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用作为位运算知识的参考资料。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，文中被引用为位运算知识的参考资料，网址为https://oi-wiki.org/math/bit/#%E4%B8%8E%E6%88%96%E5%BC%82%E6%88%96。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，文中被引用为位运算知识的参考资料，网址为https://oi-wiki.org/math/bit/#%E4%B8%8E%E6%88%96%E5%BC%82%E6%88%96。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料，网址为https://oi-wiki.org/math/bit/#%E4%B8%8E%E6%88%96%E5%BC%82%E6%88%96。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料，具有权威性与教育性。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料，网址为https://oi-wiki.org/math/bit/#%E4%B8%8E%E6%88%96%E5%BC%82%E6%88%96。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料。"&lt;SEP&gt;"OI-Wiki是一个提供信息学竞赛相关知识的在线资源平台，被引用为位运算知识的参考资料。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c32b07be1497200073fc0ef9c06b5453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f831b89c29a24b6f937f910e69eb76a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aec8259c8baec36c3dade3722427d1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57add46cc4c97ae41d878b651704f581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e931acf8bba8e661f930fa1ad11ddc08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7433253258a222d25e3dedd5ea73b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5eb1d8406f1c61b5ad1590b8396b2ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;硝基甲苯之袭&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"硝基甲苯之袭 是本题的标题或情境命名，代表小苯所面临的算法挑战事件，涉及异或与最大公约数的数学关系。"&lt;SEP&gt;"硝基甲苯之袭 是本题的标题或题目名称，描述了小苯面临的计算问题，即在数组中寻找满足异或等于最大公约数的元素对。"&lt;SEP&gt;"硝基甲苯之袭是本题的标题，代表一个关于数组中元素对满足异或等于最大公约数条件的算法问题场景。"&lt;SEP&gt;"硝基甲苯之袭是本题的标题，象征性地指代该算法问题的挑战性情境，与题目内容无直接语义关联，可能为命名风格或隐喻。"&lt;SEP&gt;"硝基甲苯之袭是本题的标题，指代小苯所面对的计算问题，即在数组中寻找满足异或等于最大公约数的元素对的计数任务。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0f831b89c29a24b6f937f910e69eb76a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A_I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"a_i denotes the i-th element in the array of integers, where i ranges from 1 to n, and each value is subject to the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j) for valid pairs."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i represents an element in the array at index i, used in the mathematical condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j). It is a variable denoting a specific integer value from the input array."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i represents an element in the array at index i, used in the mathematical condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j). It is a variable in the algorithmic problem posed to 小苯."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i denotes the i-th element in the integer array, acting as a variable point in a numerical space. It is a conceptual geometric entity in the problem’s mathematical domain, with values subject to constraints implied by the XOR-GCD condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i represents an element in the array at index i, used in the mathematical condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j). It is a variable placeholder for array elements in the problem statement."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i denotes the i-th element of the sequence, each independently and uniformly randomly generated within the interval [l_i, r_i], forming the core variable set in the Absolute Expectation problem."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i represents the i-th element in the sequence, a randomly generated integer variable within the interval [l_i, r_i], central to the computation of the sequence's value."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i represents the i-th element in the sequence, a random integer variable whose value is drawn independently and uniformly from the interval [l_i, r_i]. It is a mathematical entity acting as a variable in the sequence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0f831b89c29a24b6f937f910e69eb76a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f207867e95527d1c21eb90640d585ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A_J&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"a_j denotes the j-th element in the array of integers, where j &gt; i, and it forms a pair with a_i to evaluate the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_j represents an element in the array at index j (where j &gt; i), paired with a_i to satisfy the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j). It is a variable in the algorithmic problem posed to 小苯."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_j represents an element in the array at index j (where j &gt; i), used in the mathematical condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j). It is a variable denoting another specific integer value from the input array."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_j denotes the j-th element in the integer array (where j &gt; i), functioning as a second variable point in the same numerical space as a_i. Its relationship with a_i is defined by the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_j represents an element in the array at index j (where j &gt; i), used in the mathematical condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j). It is a variable placeholder for array elements in the problem statement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0f831b89c29a24b6f937f910e69eb76a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GCD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"gcd (greatest common divisor) is a mathematical function referenced in the problem to compute the largest positive integer that divides two numbers without remainder, central to the problem’s constraint."&lt;SEP&gt;"gcd (greatest common divisor) is a mathematical function referenced in the problem to define the relationship between two integers, used to validate valid pairs (a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"gcd stands for greatest common divisor, a mathematical function used to compute the largest positive integer that divides two numbers without remainder. It is central to the problem's condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"gcd stands for greatest common divisor, a mathematical function used to compute the largest positive integer that divides two numbers without remainder. It is central to the problem's constraint."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f831b89c29a24b6f937f910e69eb76a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"xor (bitwise exclusive OR) is a binary operation used in the problem to compare bit patterns of two integers, forming the left-hand side of the key equation a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"xor (exclusive OR) is a bitwise operation referenced in the problem to define the relationship between two integers, used to validate valid pairs (a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"xor stands for bitwise exclusive OR, a binary operation used in the problem to compare bits of two integers. It is a core component of the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"xor stands for bitwise exclusive OR, a binary operation used in the problem to compare two integers bit-by-bit. It is the other key operator in the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f831b89c29a24b6f937f910e69eb76a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CNT[M]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"cnt[M] is a frequency-counting array that tracks occurrences of each unique value in the input. It acts as a statistical map over the numerical space, enabling optimized pair counting."&lt;SEP&gt;"cnt[M] is an array in the student's program used to count occurrences of each integer value in the input array, enabling efficient lookup during pair counting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CNT[]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"cnt[] is an array in the student's code used to count the frequency of each integer value in the input array. It enables efficient computation of valid pairs by avoiding redundant iterations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A[]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"a[] is the main input array in the student's code, storing the n integers provided as input. It is sorted and deduplicated to optimize the search for valid (a_i, a_j) pairs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2025-01-21 15:23:04&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This timestamp marks the exact recording time of the error report, indicating when the incorrect student submission was logged and analyzed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;32-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"32-1 is the unique record identifier for this specific student submission and error report, used for tracking and referencing in an automated grading or debugging system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GCD(A_I, A_J)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"gcd(a_i, a_j) is the greatest common divisor of two array elements, representing a derived numerical point that must equal their XOR result. It is a mathematical construct that constrains the valid pairs (a_i, a_j) in the solution space."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A_I XOR A_J&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"a_i xor a_j is the bitwise XOR result of two array elements, acting as a computed value that must match the gcd of the same pair. It defines a transformational relationship between two points in the numerical space."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;双生数组&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"双生数组是一个数学概念事件，指大小为偶数、恰好包含两种不同元素且每种元素出现次数相同的数组，是题目要求转换的目标状态。"&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组是一个数学概念事件，指大小为偶数、恰好包含两种不同元素且每种元素出现次数相同的数组，是题目要求转换的目标状态。"&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组是一个数学概念事件，指大小为偶数、恰好包含两种不同元素且每种元素出现次数相同的数组，是题目要求转换的目标状态。"&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组是一个由小红定义的数组结构事件，要求数组大小为偶数、恰好包含两种不同元素且每种元素出现次数相等，是题目要求达成的目标状态。"&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组是一个由小红定义的数组结构事件，要求数组长度为偶数、恰好包含两种不同元素、且每种元素出现次数相等，是题目要达成的目标状态。"&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组是一个数学概念事件，指大小为偶数、恰好包含两种不同元素且每种元素出现次数相等的数组，是题目要求转换的目标状态。"&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组是一个数学概念事件，指长度为偶数、恰好包含两种不同元素且每种元素出现次数相同的数组，是题目要求转换的目标状态。"&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组是一个由小红定义的数学概念，指大小为偶数、恰好包含两种不同元素且每种元素出现次数相等的数组，是题目要求转换的目标状态。"&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组是一个数学概念事件，指长度为偶数、恰好包含两种不同元素且每种元素出现次数相等的数组，是题目要求转换的目标状态。"&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组是一个由小红定义的数组结构事件，要求数组大小为偶数、恰好包含两种不同元素且每种元素出现次数相等，是题目要达成的目标状态。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c2a57305752e3a687103dd58dbee53bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7230c75a37c25448800f6f28d89050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ac191ac64f16e456c655d4b8863811&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8796025571904280b91872c5eb3f6610&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e091fd25a6ba2509fa168c85c52636ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad8afc7ac300d86b72e962805041fa5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29764514e79d905f57239a2bf826b46d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0be1ff21d6f00384f294e712dc03c7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47baadad1b80a9eb7ea15b9cd824968b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44c8edff064a63bf1c338d7c234b2385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d45a376c5f8e29b656fb8024a9e1fab6</data>
    </node>
