    <node id="&quot;TOKITSUKAZE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tokitsukaze is a character who rides a dragon and can unleash a special ability called 'Dragon's Breath' to defeat monsters on a grid map."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tokitsukaze is a character who rides a dragon and can unleash a special attack called 'Dragon's Breath' on a grid map to defeat monsters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tokitsukaze is a character who rides a dragon and can use a special ability called 'Dragon's Breath' to defeat monsters on a grid map."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tokitsukaze is a character who rides a dragon and can unleash a special attack called 'Dragon's Breath' to eliminate monsters on a grid map."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tokitsukaze is a character who rides a dragon and uses the 'Dragon's Breath' ability to eliminate monsters on a grid map by targeting coordinates and activating a diagonal 'X'-shaped flame pattern."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tokitsukaze is a character who rides a dragon and uses the 'Dragon's Breath' ability to eliminate monsters on a grid map by creating an 'X'-shaped flame pattern."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tokitsukaze is a person associated with a mathematical problem involving a sequence of random integers and the computation of the expected value of the absolute difference sum between consecutive elements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tokitsukaze is a person associated with a mathematical problem involving the expectation of the absolute difference sum in a randomly generated integer sequence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tokitsukaze is a person associated with a mathematical problem involving a sequence of random integers and the calculation of the expected value of the absolute difference sum between consecutive elements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tokitsukaze is a person associated with a mathematical problem involving the expected value of the absolute difference sum of a randomly generated integer sequence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tokitsukaze is a person associated with a mathematical problem involving the expected value of a sequence's absolute difference sum, where each element is randomly generated within a given interval."</data>
