    <node id="&quot;ABSOLUTE EXPECTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Absolute Expectation is the mathematical event or problem of computing the expected value of the absolute difference sum across consecutive elements in a randomly generated sequence, as posed in the problem statement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Absolute Expectation is the mathematical event or problem of computing the expected value of the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements in a randomly generated sequence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Absolute Expectation is the mathematical problem or challenge posed by Tokitsukaze, centered on computing the expected value of val(a) = sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements in a randomly generated sequence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Absolute Expectation refers to the mathematical problem of computing the expected value of val(a), the sum of absolute differences in a randomly generated sequence, as posed in the problem titled 'Tokitsukaze and Absolute Expectation'."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f207867e95527d1c21eb90640d585ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52425facb0b31d12436db806ca0992de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L_I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"l_i is the left boundary of the i-th query subinterval [l_i, r_i], used to define the segment of the permutation to be sorted."&lt;SEP&gt;"l_i is the lower bound of the interval from which the i-th element a_i is randomly generated; it defines a constraint on the possible values of a_i in the sequence."&lt;SEP&gt;"l_i is the lower bound of the interval from which the i-th element a_i is randomly generated; it is a mathematical parameter, not a geographic location, but 'geo' is the only available non-person/organization type."&lt;SEP&gt;"l_i is the lower bound of the interval from which the i-th sequence element a_i is randomly generated, defining a geometric constraint on possible values."&lt;SEP&gt;"l_i represents the left boundary of a subinterval [l_i, r_i] in a permutation query, used to define the range of elements to be sorted."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae03b8ab8904bfd565e3a28acd596fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f207867e95527d1c21eb90640d585ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bbd9f3652366c894d3ef5e4694e35b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;R_I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"r_i is the right boundary of the i-th query subinterval [l_i, r_i], used to define the segment of the permutation to be sorted."&lt;SEP&gt;"r_i is the upper bound of the interval from which the i-th element a_i is randomly generated; it defines a constraint on the possible values of a_i in the sequence."&lt;SEP&gt;"r_i is the upper bound of the interval from which the i-th element a_i is randomly generated; it is a mathematical parameter, not a geographic location, but 'geo' is the only available non-person/organization type."&lt;SEP&gt;"r_i is the upper bound of the interval from which the i-th sequence element a_i is randomly generated, defining a geometric constraint on possible values alongside l_i."&lt;SEP&gt;"r_i represents the right boundary of a subinterval [l_i, r_i] in a permutation query, used to define the range of elements to be sorted."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae03b8ab8904bfd565e3a28acd596fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f207867e95527d1c21eb90640d585ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bbd9f3652366c894d3ef5e4694e35b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAL(A)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"val(a) is the defined mathematical function representing the total absolute difference between consecutive elements in the sequence, used to compute the expected value."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is the defined value function of the sequence, computed as the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements, which is the quantity whose expectation is being calculated."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is the value function of the sequence defined as the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements: ∑|a_{i-1} - a_i| for i from 2 to n. It is the quantity whose expectation is being computed."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is the event or computed quantity defined as the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements in the sequence, i.e., ∑|a_{i-1} - a_i| for i from 2 to n."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is the event or computed quantity defined as the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements in the sequence, i.e., ∑|a_{i-1} - a_i| for i from 2 to n, whose expectation is the problem's objective."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-52425facb0b31d12436db806ca0992de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-643a1dae351fde67dd0b6b4bafe4269b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f207867e95527d1c21eb90640d585ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"mod is a constant set to 1e9 + 7 in the student's program, serving as a modular arithmetic constraint to prevent integer overflow and standardize computational results within a defined numerical system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pow is a function in the student program that computes modular exponentiation, used to calculate modular inverses for division under modulo arithmetic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pow is a function in the student's program that computes modular exponentiation, used to calculate modular inverses and handle division under modulo arithmetic, acting as a structural component of the computational framework."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pow is a function in the student program that computes modular exponentiation, used to calculate modular inverses, particularly for dividing by (R[i] - L[i] + 1) * (R[i - 1] - L[i - 1] + 1) under modulo arithmetic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pow is a helper function in the student program that computes modular exponentiation, used to calculate modular inverses for division under modulo arithmetic."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f207867e95527d1c21eb90640d585ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52425facb0b31d12436db806ca0992de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-643a1dae351fde67dd0b6b4bafe4269b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"query is a function in the student program that computes the expected absolute difference between two sequence elements a_{i-1} and a_i using inclusion-exclusion over their respective intervals [l_i, r_i]."&lt;SEP&gt;"query is a function in the student program that uses the solve function to compute the expected absolute difference between two intervals [L_i, R_i] and [L_j, R_j] using inclusion-exclusion, but is incorrectly implemented."&lt;SEP&gt;"query is a function in the student's program that uses the solve function to compute the expected absolute difference between two sequence elements using inclusion-exclusion over their intervals, serving as a key computational unit."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f207867e95527d1c21eb90640d585ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-643a1dae351fde67dd0b6b4bafe4269b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L[M]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"L[M] is an array in the student program storing the lower bounds l_i for each sequence element a_i, indexed from 1 to n, used in the query function for interval arithmetic."&lt;SEP&gt;"L[M] is an array in the student's program storing the lower bounds l_i for each sequence element, acting as a data structure to organize input constraints."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-643a1dae351fde67dd0b6b4bafe4269b</data>
    </node>
