      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"R[M] is an array in the student program storing the upper bounds r_i for each sequence element a_i, indexed from 1 to n, used alongside L[M] in the query function."&lt;SEP&gt;"R[M] is an array in the student's program storing the upper bounds r_i for each sequence element, acting as a data structure to organize input constraints alongside L[M]."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-643a1dae351fde67dd0b6b4bafe4269b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEQUENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sequence refers to the ordered set of n randomly generated integers {a_1, a_2, ..., a_n} that forms the core object of analysis in the problem."</data>
