    <node id="&quot;TIC-TAC-TOE GAME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A 3x3 tic-tac-toe game between 小L and 炸鸡, where the board is in a drawn state with equal moves, and it is 小L's turn with a one-time privilege to make two consecutive moves."&lt;SEP&gt;The tic-tac-toe game is a 3x3 grid-based strategic contest between 小L and 炸鸡, where the objective is to be the first to place three of one’s marks in a row, column, or diagonal. The game is currently in an unresolved, balanced state, with both players having made an equal number of moves and no winner yet determined. It is now 小L’s turn, and under a special rule, 小L possesses a one-time privilege to make two consecutive moves during this turn. This double-move (or two-move) privilege introduces a unique strategic dynamic to the game, distinguishing it from standard tic-tac-toe rules. Despite the equal number of moves and the absence of a winner, the game remains active and undecided, with the outcome contingent on how 小L leverages this special opportunity.&lt;SEP&gt;"The tic-tac-toe game is a 3x3 grid-based strategic game between 小L and 炸鸡, where the goal is to get three marks in a row, column, or diagonal; the game is currently in a paused state with equal moves and no winner yet, and it is 小L's turn with a special double-move privilege."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tic-tac-toe game is a 3x3 board game between 小L and 炸鸡, where the goal is to get three of one's marks in a row, column, or diagonal. The game is in a drawn state with equal moves made by both players, and it is now 小L's turn with a special double-move privilege."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'G' represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has placed a mark yet. It is a state marker within the game grid."&lt;SEP&gt;"'G' represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has placed a mark yet; it is a state indicator within the game's grid system."&lt;SEP&gt;"G represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has placed a mark yet."&lt;SEP&gt;"G represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has placed a mark yet; it is part of the game state representation using the notation s_{i,j}."&lt;SEP&gt;The symbol "G" represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where neither player has placed a mark yet. It serves as a state identifier or state marker within the game’s grid system, denoting unoccupied locations that are available for future moves. "G" is used to track the current game state, and its presence signifies that a cell remains playable. When all cells are occupied by either player’s marks, no "G" cells remain on the board. The term "G" is synonymous with an unoccupied or empty cell and is consistently applied across all descriptions as a fundamental component of the tic-tac-toe game’s spatial representation.&lt;SEP&gt;"G represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has placed a mark yet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-031bf50845b77cce37dae6bb7e48b3a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bb705f581ef523c90424ea77cfe827&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0414d324dc902fa7bfe392b580d12b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fc62282a1bad52fcf26a22bb1d2063&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e8674c89c2bbd80ac2ed7bf4f4ece7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9096db2ee9b817fdd4447c67ca4e24c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a625df4ed1e048ecc8681beebcec0a9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'O' represents a mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating ownership of a cell in the 3x3 grid."&lt;SEP&gt;"'O' represents a mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating ownership of a cell in the 3x3 grid; it is one of two player symbols used in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"O represents a mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating one of the opponent's chosen positions."&lt;SEP&gt;The symbol "O" represents a move made by 炸鸡 on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating ownership or occupation of a specific cell (i,j) within the grid. It is one of the two player symbols used in the game, the other being "X", and serves as a fundamental component of the game state to track each player’s claimed positions. "O" is consistently described as the marker associated with 炸鸡, used to denote their chosen moves throughout gameplay, and plays a critical role in determining potential winning lines. While some descriptions refer to "O" as representing “the opponent’s moves,” this is contextually inaccurate if 炸鸡 is the player using "O"; therefore, these references are resolved to mean that "O" is the symbol used by 炸鸡 themselves — not their opponent — and any mention of “opponent” is likely a misstatement or confusion in perspective. In summary, "O" is a symbolic representation of 炸鸡’s selections on the board, essential for evaluating progress and outcome in the game.&lt;SEP&gt;"O represents a mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating one of the opponent's moves in the game."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-031bf50845b77cce37dae6bb7e48b3a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bb705f581ef523c90424ea77cfe827&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0414d324dc902fa7bfe392b580d12b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fc62282a1bad52fcf26a22bb1d2063&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e8674c89c2bbd80ac2ed7bf4f4ece7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9096db2ee9b817fdd4447c67ca4e24c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a625df4ed1e048ecc8681beebcec0a9e</data>
    </node>
