      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 3x3 grid is the playing field of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of 9 cells arranged in 3 rows and 3 columns, identified by coordinates (i,j), where i and j range from 1 to 3."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing field of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of 9 cells arranged in 3 rows and 3 columns, identified by coordinates (i,j), where i and j range from 1 to 3."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing field of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of 9 cells arranged in 3 rows and 3 columns, where players place their marks."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing field of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of nine cells identified by coordinates (i,j), where i is the row (1 to 3) and j is the column (1 to 3). Each cell can hold 'X', 'O', or 'G' to represent moves or empty spaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing field of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of 9 cells arranged in 3 rows and 3 columns. Each cell is identified by coordinates (i,j) and can hold state X, O, or G."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing field of tic-tac-toe, composed of 9 cells identified by coordinates (i,j), where i is the row and j is the column. It defines the spatial structure of the game."</data>
