    <edge source="&quot;STUDENT PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;GCD&quot;">
      <data key="d3">14.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Student Program computes gcd values implicitly by iterating over divisors of a[i] to satisfy the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Student Program uses the concept of gcd implicitly by iterating over divisors of a[i], but fails to correctly compute or relate it to xor."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;STUDENT PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;XOR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">17.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Student Program uses the xor operator to compare values and check the condition a_i xor a_j == gcd(a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Student Program uses xor operation in its condition (a[i] ^ j), but incorrectly applies it by not ensuring j is gcd(a[i], a[i]^j), leading to logical error."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
